
Channeled attacks, colloquially known as "wind-ups", are sometimes used by creatures and denizens throughout the sector in an attempt to win a fight. They are slow and, if allowed to complete, can be lethal.
 
Fortunately for you, there are ways to interrupt these wind-ups. The options are different for each class - it's recommended you learn these moves as soon as possible, since windup attacks start showing up in the game as early as level 12.
The neural_blinder artifact auto-interrupts windups every twenty seconds.
CLASS INTERRUPT ABILITIES
------------------------------
BEAST
   -MWP NETLAUNCH. To use, do MWP NETLAUNCH <target>.
   -PLASMACASTING SEAR. To use, do PLASMA SEAR <target>.
   -PLASMACASTING FLASH. To use do PLASMA FLASH <target>.
   -SUIT RUMBLE. To use, do SUIT RUMBLE. (This is an AOE interrupt and will aggro other mobs in the room)
 
ENGINEER
   -BOTS SWING. To use, do BOT SWING <target>.
 
FURY
   -FULMINATION FEVER. To use, do KITH FEVER <target>.
   -RAGE STUN. To use, RAGE STUN <target>.
 
NANOSEER
   -NANOTECH EYESTRIKE. To use, do NANO EYESTRIKE <target>.
   -OBLIVION QUAKE. To use, do OBLIVION QUAKE. (This is an AOE interrupt and will aggro other mobs in the room)
 
SCOUNDREL
   -GUNSLINGING POINTBLANK. To use, do GUN POINTBLANK <target>.
   -GUILE POCKETSAND. To use, do GUILE POCKETSAND <target>.
   -GUILE BIND. To use, do GUILE BIND <target>. (Note: target must be prone)
                                                                
ANY
    -Hitting a leg with a limb specific attack while your target has the affliction "weak knees".